Venus shortwave spectral file, 280 bands, 0.175-20 microns
==========================================================

Recipe for sp_sw_280_je_venus: 13 gases (H2O, CO2, SO2, N2, CO, OCS, H2S,
HDO, HCl, HF, cis-OSSO, trans-OSSO, OSO-S), H2O-H2O and CO2-CO2 continua,
and five aerosol slots holding the Venus cloud modes. The p-T grid,
data/gases/ptVenus, runs from 3.3e-6 to 9.2e6 Pa and 92 to 781 K.

Environment
-----------
VENUS_SW_WORK   work directory; line-by-line files go in lbl/, k files and
                the spectral file in sp/
LINE_DATA_DIR   directory holding the line lists listed below
VENUS_SW_PROCS  OpenMP threads per Ccorr_k call (each script has a default)

Container and build
-------------------
podman_socrates   runs a command (or a shell) in the lfric_dev container
build             builds SOCRATES: ./podman_socrates ./build
check_corr_k      checks corr_k and prep_spec against examples/corr_k
check_je_file     runs a spectral file (the JE file by default) through
                  l_run_cdf and compares with JE's stored output:
                  ./check_je_file <je_ref_dir> [spectral file]
num_diff          number-by-number comparison of two text files
compare_sp        block-by-block comparison of two spectral files:
                  ./compare_sp <reference file> <new file>
column_summary    band-summed fluxes and heating rates of column runs,
                  side by side: ./column_summary <dir> [<dir> ...]

Spectral file
-------------
env_sw_280_venus             paths, maximum absorber paths, data file names;
                             the UV absorber switch VENUS_UV_ABSORBER, haus
                             (default), crisp or ph, and the spectral file
                             each uses: sp_sw_280_venus_<absorber>
mk_sp_sw_280_je_venus_skel   skeleton: bands, gases, continua, aerosols
mk_<gas>_lbl_sw_280_je_venus line-by-line absorption for one gas (slow)
mk_sp_sw_280_je_venus        k-terms from the line-by-line files, then the
                             spectral file
mk_sp_je_gaps                the same, as sp_sw_280_je_venus_gaps: no CO2 in
                             the 13 bands where the JE file has none; for
                             comparison with the JE file only
run_scatter                  Mie optics of the cloud modes -> .mon files;
                             modes 1 and 2 75% acid, modes 2' and 3 95.6%;
                             the soluble slot as VENUS_UV_ABSORBER selects
mk_uv_absorber               UV absorber of Crisp (1986): absorption only,
                             in the "soluble" slot -> uv_absorber.mon, and
                             its column profile crisp_uv_absorber.wtsol
crisp1986_uv_absorber.txt    Crisp (1986) Table IV, absorption efficiency
                             of the UV absorber in 21 intervals
mk_ph_refract                UV absorber of Perez-Hoyos et al. (2018) in
                             mode 1: 75% acid with a Gaussian added to m_i
                             (peak 1.36e-2 at 0.34 um, FWHM 0.14 um)
                             -> refract_sulphuric_75_ph, and the 5 nm
                             wavelength grid wl_venus_uv for Cscatter -w
mk_haus_uv_absorber          UV absorber of Haus et al. (2015): absorption
                             only, in the "soluble" slot ->
                             haus_uv_absorber.mon, and its column profile
                             haus_uv_absorber.wtsol (58-70 km, optical
                             depth 0.205 at 0.35 um)
haus2015_uv_absorber.txt     Haus et al. (2015) Fig. 18 absorber
                             cross-section, as the Venus PCM tabulates it
run_scatter_acid             the same Mie optics with every mode made of
                             acid of one refractive index file
refract_sulphuric_75_pw, refract_sulphuric_84p5, refract_sulphuric_95p6
                             refractive index of 75, 84.5 and 95.6%
                             sulphuric acid at 300 K (Palmer & Williams
                             1975, Appl. Opt. 14, 208), on the wavelengths
                             of data/aerosol/refract_sulphuric
acid_test                    column runs with the cloud at each of the
                             three concentrations:
                             ./podman_socrates ./acid_test <je_ref_dir>
cis-OSSO.uvxsc, trans-OSSO.uvxsc, OSO-S.uvxsc, pt_single
                             UV cross-sections for the OSSO isomers
mk_sp_sw_280_venus_skel      skeleton of our own file: as the JE skeleton
                             with SO, S3 and S4 (gases 111-113) added and
                             the OSSO isomers left out
mk_sp_sw_280_venus           assembles our own file, sp_sw_280_venus_<absorber>, from
                             the k files of mk_sp_sw_280_je_venus and
                             mk_uv_sw_280_venus and the .mon files of
                             run_scatter, then makes the strongest absorber
                             of each band its major gas with tidy_90:
                             ./podman_socrates ./mk_sp_sw_280_venus
mk_so_uvxsc                  SO UV cross-sections (Heays et al. 2023), 12
                             temperatures -> so.uvxsc (250 MB, not in git;
                             kept at $VENUS_SW_WORK/uv/so.uvxsc). Needs
                             numpy and h5py:
                             ./mk_so_uvxsc <Heays data dir> [output file]
mk_co2_uvxsc                 CO2 UV cross-sections (Venot et al. 2018), 10
                             temperatures, gaps filled with the paper's
                             continuum formula -> co2_uv.uvxsc:
                             ./mk_co2_uvxsc <Venot data dir>
pt_so_uv, pt_co2_uv          the record temperatures, for the look-up fits
mk_s3s4_uvxsc                S3 and S4 visible cross-sections (Billmers &
                             Smith 1991; S3 beyond 475 nm Krasnopolsky 1987
                             x 1.4, as Krasnopolsky 2013) -> s3.uvxsc,
                             s4.uvxsc: ./mk_s3s4_uvxsc
mk_uv_sw_280_venus           k-terms of SO (bands 3-15), CO2 UV (bands
                             1-11), S3 (bands 36-85) and S4 (bands 51-80):
                             ./podman_socrates ./mk_uv_sw_280_venus
                             [first SO band] [last SO band]

Column runs
-----------
mk_venus_atm            venus_atm_obs_so2.raw, the S3 and S4 profiles,
                        the haus_mode* cloud
                        profiles, the UV absorber's profiles (crisp:
                        crisp_uv_absorber.wtsol; ph: mode 1 split into
                        ph_mode1_lower.soot and ph_mode1_upper.wtsol;
                        haus: haus_uv_absorber.wtsol) and
                        so_vpcm_day.so -> venus.<suffix> netCDF inputs
mk_so_column            SO profile of the column -> so_vpcm_day.so, from
                        so_day_mean_vpcm.txt (Venus PCM day mean)
mk_s3s4_column          S3 and S4 profiles of the column (Krasnopolsky
                        2013: 11 and 4 ppt below 10 km, 18 and 6 ppt at
                        10-19 km, none above) -> s3_kras13.s3,
                        s4_kras13.s4; prints their column amounts
mk_haus_cloud           cloud profiles of the Haus et al. (2016) standard
                        model, all four modes -> haus_mode1.soot,
                        haus_mode2.sulph, haus_modep.oceanic,
                        haus_mode3.ash, and mode 1 split at 65 km ->
                        ph_mode1_lower.soot, ph_mode1_upper.wtsol (the
                        part above 65 km scaled to optical depth 3.2 at
                        0.63 um, as Perez-Hoyos et al. 2018); with a
                        spectral file as argument
                        prints each mode's optical depth at 1 micron:
                        ./mk_haus_cloud [spectral file]
planet.nml              Venus constants for Cl_run_cdf -N
run_column_venus        one column with the mk_venus_atm inputs and any
                        spectral file (ours by default), output as CDL
                        text in VENUS_SW_WORK/column/<tag>:
                        ./podman_socrates ./run_column_venus <tag> [file]
                        [zenith angle, degrees, 51 by default]
run_column_sweep        run_column_venus at mu = 0.05, 0.10, ..., 1.00 and
                        at 45 and 65.6 degrees, for global and zonal means:
                        ./podman_socrates ./run_column_sweep <tag> [file]
Run: Cl_run_cdf -N planet.nml -B venus -s sp_sw_280_je_venus -R 1 280 -S
     -r -g 4 -u -C 5 -ch 280 -a

Line lists (not in git)
-----------------------
HITRAN2020 (doi:10.1016/j.jqsrt.2021.107949). .par: air-broadened,
downloaded 2022-10-27 (H2S 2022-11-15). .bpar: bespoke format, all CO2
isotopologues with self-broadening, 2022-11-15. .par_co2: CO2-broadened,
2022-11-15. .bpar and .par_co2 are read with Ccorr_k -BD, .par with -D.

